        "text_YYjgFV": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Rená Doniger, President of NADCO Tapes & Labels, grew up in a family business, where her parents owned and operated a tree and crane service company in New Hampshire. This early exposure to the dynamics of running a family business gave her a deep understanding of the complexities involved at a young age. Rená’s passion for accounting and systems led her to pursue a Bachelor’s degree in Accounting from Southern New Hampshire University.</p><p>When she joined the company alongside Neil, she quickly took the reins, identifying key areas for improvement and implementing systems designed to ensure long-term success. One of her early contributions was introducing programs that enabled the design, pre-press, and production teams to consistently fulfill customer orders with precision. This foundational work played a crucial role in the company’s continued success.</p><p>In 1993, NADCO took out its first business loan of $80,000, marking a significant milestone in Rena’s journey with the company. From this point, she became fully invested in the success of the business. A year later, in 1994, Rená and Neil welcomed their daughter Alicia, followed by their son Jared in 1996. Juggling family, business, and marriage has been a challenge Rená has mastered with Neil’s unwavering support. Together, they have become a true “Yin and Yang” couple, a dynamic that was noted at an exclusive retreat a few years ago.</p>",
            "subtext_color": true
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "badge_rTMetq",
