    "rich_text_KckTAy": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "text_i3qdf3": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>As the business grew, the need for more space became apparent. In 2000, they built their first facility in New Hampshire. Soon after, Rená recognized the opportunity to expand the business and her own role within it, which led to the decision to relocate. In 2005, NADCO officially moved to Sarasota, Florida. This move was not only a professional challenge but also a personal one, as Rená managed the relocation of both the business and her family. Finding the land, securing a new location, and supporting her growing family during this transition was no small task, but Rená embraced it fully.</p><p>Relocating the business and expanding her role as president brought new challenges, but Rena remained committed to maintaining strong relationships with both employees and customers. Her dedication to never taking a step backward and her constant drive for progress continue to shape NADCO’s vision. Rená has fully embraced Neil’s vision for the company and has worked tirelessly to bring it to fruition, always with a deep passion for the business and its potential.In the early days, Rená and Neil worked closely together to write the company’s catalog, and she even contributed to the design work. Her comprehensive knowledge of the product, the process, and the end result allows her to see the bigger picture and guide the company toward success.Rená is often accompanied by her beloved French bulldogs, Charlie and Stella, a familiar sight at the office. Above all, she is most proud of her family and cherishes time spent with her husband, children, parents, and friends. Her greatest accomplishment, she says, is raising her children.</p>",
            "text_size": "text-base",
            "text_line_limit": "none",
            "button_style": "btn--underline",
            "button_icon": "none"
          }
        }
